{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IntervalTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Bound"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bound"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Stein, "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Introduction to Algorithms","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with different values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"],"type":"codeListing"